    @tableofcontents

    @section ncursesapilifecycle Lifecycle and Data Types

    |!API|!Purpose
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Session "Session"|Terminal ownership, colors, cursor, input injection, and cleanup
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Window "Window"|Drawing surface, geometry, text inspection, and input events
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Panel "Panel"|Overlapping windows with explicit stacking order
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::TestTerminal "TestTerminal"|Pseudo-terminal for automated tests
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Ansi "Ansi"|SGR text parsing, display-width measurement, and wrapping
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Style "Style"|Foreground, background, and attribute values
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::InputEvent "InputEvent"|Typed keyboard, mouse, and resize event data
    |@ref Qore::Ncurses::Size "Size" and @ref Qore::Ncurses::Position "Position"|Terminal rows/columns and coordinates

    Obtain the screen with @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::screen() "Session::screen()" or create a
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window "Window" with explicit dimensions. Close the session after its
    windows and panels are no longer in use. See @ref ncurses_quickstartguide "Quick Start".

    @section ncursesapidrawing Selecting a Drawing Method

    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawText() "Window::drawText()": draw at a row and column.
    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextClipped() "Window::drawTextClipped()": clip to surface bounds.
    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextInside() "Window::drawTextInside()": preserve a border.
    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawTextInsideLine() "Window::drawTextInsideLine()": clear and replace an inner line.
    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::clearInsideLine() "Window::clearInsideLine()": erase an inner line.
    - @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawAnsiText() "Window::drawAnsiText()" and
      @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::drawAnsiTextInsideLine() "Window::drawAnsiTextInsideLine()": render SGR colors.

    See @ref ncurses_stylesguide "Style System" and @ref ncurses_ansiguide "ANSI SGR Text"
    for complete examples. @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::readEvent() "Window::readEvent()" handles
    input separately; event handling is explained in @ref ncurses_mouseguide "Mouse Support".

    @section ncursesapirefresh Batched Refresh and Cursor Ownership

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::refresh() "Window::refresh()" updates one window immediately.
    For multiple surfaces, queue each update with
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::noutrefresh() "Window::noutrefresh()", update panel stacking with
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::updatePanels() "Session::updatePanels()", and call
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Session::doupdate() "Session::doupdate()" once. This avoids flushing
    intermediate drawing states to the terminal:

    @code{.py}
%modern
%requires ncurses

Ncurses::Session session();
on_exit session.close();
Ncurses::Window window = session.screen();
window.clear();
window.drawText(0, 0, "Batched update");
window.noutrefresh();
session.updatePanels();
session.doupdate();
window.readEvent();
    @endcode

    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::setLeaveOk() "Window::setLeaveOk()" allows auxiliary windows
    to refresh without taking cursor ownership. Use
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::saveCursor() "Window::saveCursor()" and
    @ref Qore::Ncurses::Window::restoreCursor() "Window::restoreCursor()" around drawing that
    would otherwise move an input cursor. For coordinated calls from multiple threads, see
    @ref ncurses_threads "Threading".
*/
